{"duration_api_ms":116261,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b6c5af78-33bd-4eb5-9246-10b4cd03d993","total_cost_usd":0.3420124,"usage":{"input_tokens":20,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16374,"cache_read_input_tokens":218512,"output_tokens":10818,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5542},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16374},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":10818,"cacheReadInputTokens":218512,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16374,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3420124,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5542,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":10,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"A prudent agent exists with modal depth 1: **`(B(a)|B(~a))->B(F)`**, i.e. (□a ∨ □¬a) → □⊥. `check.py` reports it as prudent: it defects against CooperateBot and DefectBot and cooperates with FairBot and with itself.\n\n**Q1/Q2 – smallest depth is 1.** A depth-0 formula can't contain any atoms, because every atom has to sit inside a box. So it is built only from ⊤, ⊥ and connectives and does the same thing against every opponent. It can't both defect against CooperateBot and cooperate with FairBot, whatever its size.\n\n**Q3 – all depth-1 prudent agents, and the smallest one.**\n- **How depth 1 reduces:** a depth-1 agent's action at world n depends only on which (a, c, d) values the opponent has shown at earlier worlds. Any rule from that set of values to an action can be written as a depth-1 formula.\n- **Characterization:** working through the four games by hand shows the agent is prudent exactly when its rule gives these six values:\n  - cooperate when nothing has been seen yet (world 0);\n  - defect on {111} (CooperateBot) and on {000} (DefectBot);\n  - cooperate on {111, 110, 010} (FairBot);\n  - cooperate on {111, 000} and on {111, 000, 100} (itself).\n\n  Every other set of values is free.\n- **Smallest formula:** an exhaustive search over depth-1 formulas finds the minimum is 9 symbols with constants (the answer formula). Without constants it is 12, which fits the given evidence that nothing of 7 symbols or fewer works. I didn't check whether a deeper formula could be shorter than 9 symbols.\n\nI wrote `/work/answer.md` and then `/work/SUBMIT`, which ended the attempt for everyone. argon never posted on the board, so the answer was not agreed with them before I submitted. The search scripts are in `/work/opus/`: `minsize.py` (with constants) and `minsize_noconst.py` (without).","ttft_ms":2958,"type":"result","duration_ms":116646,"uuid":"375995b7-d7da-44d2-a57f-3b20ac30b18d","ttft_stream_ms":2543,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":2544,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
